id: pm-rlm-sdk-settings
title: Adopt revision-safe SDK settings sections
description: "Replace private RLM settings parsing and workspace mutation with public section receipts and compare-and-set writes, retaining domain validation and flag precedence."
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: concurrency,sdk-adoption,settings
created_at: "2026-11-06T12:10:09.663Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T15:21:03.703Z"
author: codex-sol
acceptance_criteria: "Real no-git SDK trackers cover stored/default receipts, typed malformed refusals, cross-process stale writes without history changes, sibling/core preservation and command/library parity."
comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T12:10:17.334Z",codex-sol,"Read companion pm-cli-website-8opm (G3) and pm-cli-website-m8dy (G4) without mutation. G4 names other packages; apply adapter-parity criteria only to RLM. Plan: SDK readSettingsSection/writeSettingsSection with read revision, typed host refusals, retained package validation/privacy, real no-git trackers and OS-process race tests. Installed pinned SDK 2026.11.4 exports both APIs; public registry currently reports 2026.11.6. No dependency bump planned."
  "2026-11-06T12:15:29.498Z",codex-sol,"Implementation replaces raw settings parsing and custom mutateWorkspaceSettings with readSettingsSection/writeSettingsSection and expectedRevision. Retained defaults, numeric/model/transport validation, flag precedence and credential-reference/privacy rules because SDK sections are domain-neutral. Preserved typed malformed/invalid SDK errors. Peer and manifest floors raised to the already pinned 2026.11.4; development pin unchanged. Targeted run: 18/18 pass; typecheck and lint pass. Revert verification runs only in disposable source copies."
  "2026-11-06T12:21:10.933Z",codex-sol,Final inspection retained the existing sanitized incomplete refusal for unexpected settings I/O failures while preserving expected SDK section errors. The malformed-data regression also uses a genuine unreadable settings document shape to verify no local path appears in the refusal. Previous isolated pm run passed both linked commands; rerunning them after this final privacy-preservation adjustment.
  "2026-11-06T12:25:22.450Z",codex-sol,"Final verification: isolated pm test passed both linked commands (6/6 settings tests; 3/3 behavioral revert groups covering all six tests). Reverting private read behavior loses typed section errors/receipts; reverting only the writer causes both cross-process stale-write refusals and both section-history regressions to fail; fixed and restored runs pass. Winner settings bytes and workspace history remain unchanged on conflict. Earlier focused suite passed 18/18. Final typecheck, lint, build, duplication (0%) and docstring (183/183 declarations) pass; strict tracker health passes. Full unchanged-threshold npm/Bun gates and bot review will run on the PR. No SDK gap encountered. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-06T13:26:05.909Z",codex-sol,"Review round 1 on 5f0003c completed with one valid finding: unexpected SDK write I/O can expose a local path. Plan: preserve expected SDK errors and sanitize unexpected writes, with a real permission-denied temp-tracker regression and a source-only revert proof. No outside-diff or nitpick findings were posted. Node 22 CI failed; retrieving its completed job log before diagnosing. Superseded local full gate stopped before editing; it is not a passing full-gate receipt."
  "2026-11-06T13:30:16.094Z",codex-sol,"Node 22 CI reported 529 passing and 3 failing test entries: a stale settings revert snippet plus its parent shallow test, and an outdated CLI malformed-settings expectation. No timeout caused these failures. Updating the legacy proof to exercise genuine unexpected settings I/O; forwarding native settings_section_* refusals through command dispatch while keeping unrelated errors sanitized. Added write-I/O sanitization and CLI/refusal parity regressions; permission failure is real and modes restore in finally. Full CI coverage printed 100 in all dimensions, but the failed suite is not a passing coverage gate."
  "2026-11-06T13:36:13.022Z",codex-sol,"Review/CI fix verification: 8/8 isolated real-SDK settings tests pass; 6/6 source-only revert groups cover all eight regressions and restore passing behavior. A genuine denied write produces sanitized incomplete, while native SDK conflicts/refusals retain their codes through library and command paths. The legacy read-I/O proof now targets the adopted reader and the same real filesystem refusal test. The corrected malformed-scope/section command test passes 1/1, and unrelated checkpoint write-error sanitization still passes 1/1. Final typecheck, lint, build, duplication (0%) and docstring (183/183) pass. Initial CI failed only migration proof/expectation entries, not its settings regressions; the failed gate is not certified. Preparing one fix push with append-only pm records, followed by fresh review and full CI."
  "2026-11-06T14:17:39.814Z",codex-sol,"Final compatibility inspection found stored-domain validation ran before explicit overrides, unlike the previous package policy. Correcting resolution order: SDK retains JSON/object section validation and native revision receipts; RLM validates defaults plus stored values plus explicit overrides, preserving formerly valid repair/override calls. Adding a real SDK/no-git regression with an invalid saved model repaired by library and actual CLI overrides, including a stored cross-field context limit. Superseded local gate stopped before edits; full gates will rerun on the next head."
  "2026-11-06T14:25:06.674Z",codex-sol,"The new compatibility regression failed before the fix by assertion: a valid explicit model override was rejected as settings_section_invalid. Resolution now applies defaults, the SDK-read raw object and explicit overrides before RLM validation. SDK retains malformed-document/non-object-section refusals; invalid resolved RLM fields keep the historical invalid code. The regression uses a legacy workspace-settings write, preserves a stored context_tokens value with output_tokens above the default context, runs the actual CLI with a model override, and repairs persisted settings via the section CAS writer. No SDK mocks or default-limit changes."
  "2026-11-06T14:43:55.368Z",codex-sol,"Compatibility fix verified: 9/9 real SDK/no-git settings regressions pass; 7/7 disposable source-only revert groups cover all nine tests and restore passing bytes. The explicit-override regression fails on the prior stored-first validation and passes with library resolution, actual CLI inference and native CAS repair. Domain invalid errors retain their previous code, while malformed storage/section shape retains SDK codes. Legacy domain validation, malformed-settings CLI handling and unrelated SDK-error sanitization each pass 1/1. Typecheck, lint, build, zero duplication and 183/183 docstrings pass. The ambient global-extension host skew is already documented in pm-rlm-alp8 and companion package history; project inventory is absent and global inventory confirms the external registration. No global package or dependency pin changed. Preparing the compatibility fix push and fresh final-head gates."
  "2026-11-06T14:44:55.581Z",codex-sol,"Strict health with a fresh home and system/global Git configuration disabled passes (required merge drivers included), matching the established CI-profile procedure in pm-rlm-alp8. Ambient-profile health retains the known external pm-github version-skew warning; it is not represented as a passing ambient result. Tracker history, integrity, storage and locks are valid. No duplicate follow-up was created for this already documented environment condition."
  "2026-11-06T15:09:43.557Z",codex-sol,"Review round 2 on ff001c1 found the permission-denied write fixture does not force failure for root or Windows. Valid portability finding; replacing chmod with a real filesystem type fault after the package read, restoring the exact original settings file in finally. This retains the mandatory test and revert proof instead of skipping it. Production SDK adoption code is unchanged. No outside-diff or nitpick findings were posted."
  "2026-11-06T15:21:00.334Z",codex-sol,"Review portability fix verified: the write-I/O regression now moves the original settings file aside only in the fresh fixture, substitutes a directory after the SDK read, then restores the original file and mode in finally. Failure depends on filesystem type, not chmod or user privilege. All 9/9 settings tests and 7/7 source-only revert groups pass without skips; removing only write sanitization still fails by assertion. Typecheck, lint, duplication (0%) and 183/183 docstrings pass. Privileged and Windows execution were not measured here; no platform result is inferred as a passing runtime receipt. Production code is unchanged from ff001c1."
